title: Subscription only; API-token use must be blatantly explicit
summary: 'Founder: "i definitely want it to just use my subscrition and if there is ever a cause to use my api tokens i need it to be blatantly explicit as i dont want it to use that". Recorded as law P8-D35. Spec v3 dispatched.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#paradigm-harness'
decisions:
  - id: P8-D35
    decision: Subscription-only law. Every Claude call runs on the founder's subscription. Preflight refuses to start any session whose environment or settings would route billing to API credits (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, apiKeyHelper, custom base URLs that bill). API-token use happens only through a dedicated human-only card, approved per use, never by fallback, default or agent action; it is shown persistently in the band while active and logged as a kernel event. The budget fuse tracks the subscription's usage windows so the armada cannot lock the founder out of interactive use.
    rationale: Founder's explicit requirement.
